BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:New York Stories Series at The Mount
DTSTART:20260708T170000
DTEND:20260708T180000
DTSTAMP:20260826T123144Z
UID:7c19f8556054e26a3ba0edc6caba64@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:New York Stories is a new series of talks and live interviews 
 exploring the lives of the artists\, influencers\, and powerbrokers who ha
 ve shaped the political and cultural landscape of New York City. Through p
 ersonal stories\, pivotal moments\, and the history of institutions they b
 uilt\, challenged\, or transformed\, the series examines how these figures
  influenced New York’s past and continue to define its future. 07/08: Le
 nox to Harlem: The Life and Art of James Van Der Zee with Donna Van Der Ze
 e and Jeff L. Rosenheim 07/22: Gilded Age Fashion: Iconic Looks and the St
 ories Behind Them with Elizabeth L. Block 07/29: The Gods of New York: Joh
 nathan Mahler on Egotists\, Idealists\, Opportunists and the Birth of the 
 Modern City\, 1986-1990\, in conversation with Sarah LaDuke 08/13: Gilded 
 Lives\, Dazzling Tables: The Art of Food and Dining in Edith Wharton’s N
 ew York with Carl Raymond and Becky L. Diamond 08/26: The Talented Mrs. Ma
 ndelbaum: Margalit Fox on the Rise and Fall of an Organized Crime Boss in 
 conversation with Debby Applegate\n\nSources: The Berkshires\nEvent page: 
 https://berkshires.org/events-old/new-york-stories-series-at-the-mount/
LOCATION:The Mount\, Edith Wharton&#8217\;s Home\, 2 Plunkett Street\, Len
 ox\, MA\, 01240
URL:https://berkshires.org/events-old/new-york-stories-series-at-the-mount
 /
END:VEVENT
