BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Drawing American Stories: NRM
DTSTART:20260805T130000
DTEND:20260805T150000
DTSTAMP:20260826T123144Z
UID:ac2aa19911f12c1e7d8b0ff1872358@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:In this four-session class\, participants will be introduced t
 o the fundamental elements of drawing practice. The “classroom” will b
 e the galleries of American Stories: From Revolution to Rockwell\, the Mus
 eum’s summer exhibition commemorating the 250th anniversary of the natio
 n’s founding. Each class will focus on exploring and trying a single dra
 wing technique utilized by the various artists on view. This process of st
 udying and working directly from the work of other artists is one of the m
 ost time-honored ways artists have educated themselves and developed their
  technical skills. Materials are included\, or bring your own sketchbook. 
 Recommended for ages 16+\n\nSources: The Berkshires\nEvent page: https://b
 erkshires.org/events-old/drawing-american-stories-nrm/
LOCATION:Norman Rockwell Museum\, 9 Route 183\, Stockbridge\, MA\, 01262
