SUMMARY:Latin Night! Learn Salsa – Dance Lessons
DTSTART:20260915T182000
DTEND:20261022T213000
DTSTAMP:20260826T123144Z
UID:d8e147c9d3058701a3f9805843a720@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:💃 SALSA CLASSES ARE BACK THIS SEPTEMBER! Our next 6-week Sa
 lsa series starts September 8 & 10 at the Larcom Theatre. Choose Tuesday o
 r Thursday nights and the class that fits your experience level. BEGINNER 
 1A — FOUNDATIONS Tuesdays at 7:25 PM or Thursdays at 6:20 PM Brand new t
 o Salsa? Start here! Learn On 2 timing\, basic steps\, partner connection
 \, turns\, cross-body leads\, and foundational patterns. No previous exper
 ience necessary. BEGINNER 1B — ESSENTIALS Tuesdays at 6:20 PM or Thursda
 ys at 8:30 PM Ready for the next step? Build on the foundations from 1A wh
 ile improving timing\, connection\, leading and following technique\, tran
 sitions\, musicality\, and beginner patterns. Completion of Beginner 1A or
  equivalent experience is required. COUPLES BEGINNER 1B Tuesdays at 8:30 P
 M Want to learn together without rotating partners? This class is designed
  specifically for couples. Stay with the partner you came with while build
 ing connection\, technique\, smoother transitions\, and expanded Beginner 
 1B patterns. Beginner 1A or equivalent experience required. 6 weeks. One n
 ight a week. Lots of Salsa. We extend a special invitation for ‘leads’
  to join\, as their participation will help ensure a robust presence of po
 tential partner leads. ​ Grab your spot and join us on the dance floor t
 his September! Thelarcom.org/learnsalsa For questions about the class\, em
 ail: donnie@thelarcom.org LARCOM THEATRE\, 13 Wallis St\, Beverly MA\n\nSo
 urces: North of Boston\nEvent page: https://northofboston.org/event/latin-
 night-learn-salsa-dance-lessons/2026-09-15/
LOCATION:Larcom Theatre\, 13 Wallis Street\, Beverly\, MA\, 01915
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/latin-night-learn-salsa-dance-lessons/
 2026-09-15/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:“Brave-Too-Much”: Curator’s Remarks & Exhibit Preview
DTSTART:20260916T173000
DTEND:20260916T193000
DTSTAMP:20260826T123144Z
UID:d49e9eb7c7980203b5272167deb0ad@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:A Western exhibition at a seaside New England castle? That’s
  exactly what makes this temporary exhibition so special. Join Hammond Cas
 tle Museum for an exclusive opening celebration of “Brave-Too-Much”: T
 he Legend of John Coffee Hays\, an original temporary exhibition presented
  in partnership with the Texas Ranger Hall of Fame and Museum in Waco\, Te
 xas. Through the loan of museum artwork and fascinating stories\, this uni
 que exhibition introduces New England audiences to the legendary Texas Ran
 ger captain who was also the great-uncle and namesake of John Hays Hammond
  Jr. The exhibition traces Hays’s extraordinary journey from joining the
  Texas Rangers at just 19 years old to becoming one of the most respected 
 military leaders of his era. Notable Rangers who served under or alongside
  him include Samuel Walker\, co-inventor of the Colt Walker revolver\, the
  first practical six-shooter in the Old West\, and Flacco\, a Lipan Apache
  chief\, who gave him the nickname “Bravo-Too-Much” (aka “Brave-Too-
 Much”) for his boldness in battle. Visitors will explore his role in the
  Texas Republic\, the Mexican-American War\, the California Gold Rush\, an
 d the founding of early California communities\, while also examining the 
 complex history of the American frontier and the many cultures that shaped
  it. Evening program: 5:30 pm–6:00 pm Networking 6:00 pm–6:45 pm Prese
 ntation 6:50 pm–7:30 pm Exhibit Tours Light refreshments will be served.
  Be among the very first to experience the exhibition before it opens to t
 he public during this exclusive evening featuring: • Early access to the
  exhibition • A special curator’s presentation by Curatorial Director 
 John Leysath\, sharing the research\, stories\, and historical significanc
 e behind the exhibition • Western-inspired refreshments and themed treat
 s • Time to explore and celebrate this remarkable new exhibition with fe
 llow western history enthusiasts From the battlefields of the Texas Republ
 ic to the halls of Hammond Castle Museum\, discover the surprising family 
 connection that inspired generations and the extraordinary life of one of 
 the American frontier’s most respected leaders. Advance registration is 
 required. Museum members and VIP guests enjoy complimentary admission. Res
 ervations are required. Space is limited.\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEve
 nt page: https://northofboston.org/event/brave-too-much-curators-remarks-e
 xhibit-preview/
LOCATION:Hammond Castle Museum\, 80 Hesperus Avenue\, Gloucester\, MA\, 01
 930
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/brave-too-much-curators-remarks-exhibi
 t-preview/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:COME FROM AWAY!
DTSTART:20260916T140000
DTEND:20260916T160000
DTSTAMP:20260826T123144Z
UID:a2f13f7ce267a93f026ea308004d35@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:COME FROM AWAY is a moving and uplifting musical based on the 
 true story of what happened in the small town of Gander\, Newfoundland\, o
 n September 11\, 2001. When 38 planes carrying nearly 7\,000 passengers we
 re unexpectedly diverted there\, the residents of this isolated community 
 opened their hearts and homes to the stranded travelers. What began as a d
 ay of global tragedy transformed into a powerful tale of compassion\, conn
 ection\, and humanity. With a vibrant\, folk-inspired score and a fast-pac
 ed\, ensemble-driven narrative\, COME FROM AWAY captures the tensions\, cu
 lture clashes\, and eventual camaraderie that unfolded over several unforg
 ettable days. This Tony® Award-winning musical celebrates the best of the
  human spirit and the extraordinary capacity for good in the face of crisi
 s.\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent page: https://northofboston.org/even
 t/come-from-away/2026-09-16/1/
LOCATION:North Shore Music Theatre\, Dunham Road 54\, Beverly\, MA\, 01915
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/come-from-away/2026-09-16/1/
END:VEVENT
